<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dammam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dammam is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> coast of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and the capital of its Eastern Province. In 1938 the well Dammam No. 7, drilled by the American-owned company later known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saudi-aramco">Aramco</a>, struck the first commercial oil in the kingdom. Together with Dhahran and Khobar, Dammam has grown into a large metropolitan area and port at the centre of the Saudi oil industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dammam.jpg" alt="Dammam" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: علي عدنان الرمضان · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%B7_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%85.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
